// ---------------- Ancient ----------------
addNote("ancient", "Second urbanisation, coins and religions", `
<h3>Buddhism: names, life, councils</h3>
<ul>
<li>Buddha's epithets: <b>Shakyamuni, Tathagata</b>, Sugata, Bhagavat. <b>Nigantha Nataputta</b> = Mahavira.</li>
<li>Lumbini → Bodh Gaya (enlightenment) → Sarnath (first sermon) → Kushinagar (mahaparinibbana).</li>
<li>Councils: Rajagriha, Vaishali, Pataliputra (Ashoka), Kashmir (Kanishka, Mahayana).</li>
<li>Transmission to China: Kashyapa Matanga (67 CE), <b>Sanghabhuti</b> (late 4th century, commentary on the <b>Sarvastivada Vinaya</b>), <b>Kumarajiva</b>, Bodhidharma (Chan/Zen). Buddhaghosa's <i>Visuddhimagga</i> (Theravada, Sri Lanka).</li>
</ul>`);

addNote("ancient", "Vedic age: texts, economy and geography", `
<h3>Upanishads and Puranas</h3>
<p>Principal Upanishads (about 800–500 BCE) are full of <b>parables and dialogues</b>: Nachiketa–Yama, Satyakama Jabala, Svetaketu ("Tat tvam asi"), Yajnavalkya–Maitreyi. "Satyameva Jayate" comes from the Mundaka Upanishad. <b>Puranas</b> came later (about 300–1000 CE): 18 Mahapuranas, pancha lakshana, royal genealogies.</p>`);

